name: Gettysburg
chapter: 10
when: 1863
where: Cemetery Ridge, Pennsylvania
who: Meade's Army of the Potomac vs Lee's Army of Northern Virginia
road: dust
brief: The Union line curled from Culp's Hill round Cemetery Hill and down the ridge to the Round Tops — a fishhook three miles long that let Meade move men from one end of it to the other faster than Lee could march.
